  "summary": "An international decorative style defined by sinuous whiplash lines, botanical ornament, and the total integration of art, architecture and craft.",
  "description": "Art Nouveau sought to dissolve the boundary between fine and applied arts: buildings, furniture, jewelry, posters and tableware share one flowing, plant-derived line language. It emerged as a reaction against academic historicism and industrial standardization, drawing on the Arts and Crafts movement, Rococo and Japanese ukiyo-e prints. National variants include Jugendstil in Germany, Stile Liberty in Italy, Modernisme in Catalonia and the Vienna Secession. The style fell from favor around World War I, dismissed as expensive and impractical, but its organic line deeply influenced later design.",
